(1. PRODUCT PRINCIPLE & PERFORMANCE SPECIFICATIONS) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Superparamagnetic SPRI silica bead chemistry optimized for selective 167 bp mononucleosomal recovery.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Input volume: 0.5 mL to 5.0 mL plasma, serum, or biofluids. Protocol duration: ~45 minutes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Elution volume: 15 uL to 50 uL in Low-EDTA Tris Buffer.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. STORAGE, STABILITY & AMBIENT TRANSIT CONDITIONS) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Storage: All buffers and magnetic beads are stable at 15-25 deg C ambient temperature.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Proteinase K is lyophilized or stable at 2-8 deg C upon reconstitution.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Domestic Transit: Fully ambient shipping. No expensive dry-ice surcharge required.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. STEP-BY-STEP EXTRACTION PROTOCOL) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Step 1 \(Lysis\): Add 200 uL Lysis Buffer + 20 uL Proteinase K per 1 mL plasma. Incubate at 56 deg C for 15 min.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Step 2 \(Binding\): Add 1.2x volume of MagDNA SPRI Beads. Mix by pulse-vortexing for 10 min.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Step 3 \(Magnetic Separation\): Place tube on magnetic separator for 3 minutes. Discard clear supernatant.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Step 4 \(Washing\): Wash twice with 80% molecular biology grade ethanol. Air-dry beads for 5 minutes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Step 5 \(Elution\): Add 25 uL Elution Buffer. Incubate at room temperature for 3 min. Magnetize and collect pure cfDNA.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. COMPLIANCE & AUTHORIZED DISTRIBUTION) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Manufactured by Luminous BioSciences USA. Direct Indian distribution by Nuvamed Diagnostics LLP Limited.) Tj
0 -14 Td
